        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
          When a treadmill stops working, the instinct is to search for treadmill repair near me and
          call the first number. That can work, but it is also how owners pay a call-out fee for a
          dry deck, void a warranty that would have covered the part, or hand a motor control board
          to someone who has never opened a treadmill. The right repairer depends on two questions:
          is the machine still under warranty, and what is actually wrong with it. This guide
